  "# ADR-2607180900: .kotoba guest authoring maturity

**Status**: accepted (L1–L6 landed 2026-07-18)
**Date**: 2026-07-18
**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki

## Context

Runtime maturity (kototama R3, wasm-webcomponent browser path) is ahead of
**authoring maturity**: writers still face two grammars (`kotoba` wasm emit vs
`compiler` KIR), low-level ptr/len ABIs, sparse diagnostics, and incomplete
capability-value / package surfaces.

ADR-2607141600 recorded dual-compiler ownership and deliberately deferred
grammar reconciliation. ADR-2607171700 classifies fleet `.cljc` files; it does
**not** license ambient Clojure into the guest. This ADR is the positive plan
to raise **\"what you can write in `.kotoba`\"** without weakening confinement.

## Decision

### 1. Maturity means three columns, not one

| Column | Meaning |
|---|---|
| A. Expressiveness | Useful guests can be authored |
| B. Safety | Gates still deny ambient code/effect |
| C. Unification | One grammar catalog; backends desugar into it |

Success is never measured by \"how close to full Clojure\".

### 2. Expressiveness formula (invariant)

```text
new surface = desugar to existing primitives
            | new host capability kit (policy + negative fixture + receipt)
≠ ambient Clojure (eval/require/atom/macros/interop)
```

### 3. Shared catalog: `lang/guest-grammar.edn`

Authoritative form catalog lives in **`kotoba-lang/kotoba-lang`**:

- special forms, sugar (desugar targets), forbidden heads
- admission limits
- diagnostic hints for common author mistakes
- maturity level tags per feature

`kotoba` and `compiler` **consume** this catalog (or an embedded copy when the
git pin lags). They must not invent divergent forbidden/sugar sets silently.

### 4. Ladder L1–L6

| Level | Focus | Safety note |
|---|---|---|
| L1 | Single safe path + grammar catalog | default always gates |
| L2 | Ergonomics (string sugar, do, diagnostics) | desugar only |
| L3 | Cap values (S4b) + package admission (F-001) | least privilege for dynamic resources |
| L4 | Typed HIR (S1b) | earlier reject, not more power |
| L5 | Cross-host conformance | same guest, equal denial semantics |
| L6 | Signed modules / release evidence | supply chain |

### 5. Relationship to fleet `.cljc` migration

ADR-2607171700 remains the classification ADR. Guest authoring maturity
**feeds** that migration with a real compile surface; it does **not** require
rewriting hosts, UI, or nbb scripts into `.kotoba`.

### 6. Gap backlog (P0–P3)

| Pri | Gap | Level |
|---|---|---|
| P0 | Dual grammar / dual emit | L1 |
| P0 | Package admission residual (F-001) | L3 |
| P1 | Cap values S4b / F-003 | L3 |
| P1 | String/do sugar + diagnostics | L2 |
| P1 | Host parity matrix as conformance | L5 |
| P2 | Typed HIR S1b | L4 |
| P2 | CID guest packages (not require) | L3 |
| P2 | Selfhost analyzer authority shift | L1–L4 |
| P3 | Signed modules S5 / F-007 | L6 |
| avoid | eval/require/atom/macros/interop | — |

## Implementation notes (2026-07-18 package registry follow-up)

**Package registry (m5 first slice)**
- `kotoba.lang.package-registry`: I/O-free name@version → registry record →
  full lock dep (CID pins + signers + capabilities); `lock-from-requests`
  fail-closed
- `package-admission/resolve-lock-with-registry` admits the resolved lock
- Version-only deps still fail direct admission (registry is the only safe
  path to fill pins)
- F-001 rad scaffolding confirmed landed; kotoba#281 closed with evidence

## Implementation notes (2026-07-18 L4 + L6)

**L4 landed (typed HIR / S1b)**
- `type-system`: `[:option T]` type; bare `:nil` public returns rejected
  (`:type/no-nil-return`); prefer `[:option T]` / `[:result Ok Err]`
- `typed-hir-module` collects portable `:typed-defn` entries
- `validate-host-import-calls` + runtime surface-arity catalog (opt-in
  `:kotoba.policy/check-import-arity` / `:typed-hir`; WASM ABI params are not
  source arities)
- `require-signatures` when `:kotoba.policy/typed-hir` or
  `:kotoba.policy/require-signatures`
- type-conformance fixtures: option_result_signature, bare_nil_return

**L6 landed (signed modules / F-007)**
- `kotoba.signed-module`: Ed25519 sign/verify of guest component bytes
  (`:kotoba.signed-module/v1`); content CID+SHA256 binding; trust/revocation
- `kotoba.release-evidence`: F-007 safe-release gate requires package receipt
  + signed module + trust + key-register; SBOM/provenance required unless
  exception-register entry has `:owner` and unexpired `:expires`
- tests: `guest_maturity_l4_l6_test`

## Implementation notes (2026-07-18 L3 + L5)

**L3 landed**
- `package-contract`: `:component` kind requires real `component-cid`; optional
  `component-bytes` integrity (CID guest packages, not ambient `require`)
- `package-admission/guest-package-dep` + `admit-guest-component` + content
  mismatch → `:package/component-cid-mismatch`
- `safe-release-ready?` optional `:require-component-cid?`
- closed multi-module projects (`compile-project` / module-graph digests) remain
  the source-link path; component-cid pins the built artifact for admission
- package-conformance fixtures: positive/component-lock + missing/bad cid negatives

**L5 landed**
- `lang/host-parity.edn` v2 `:conformance` cases (JVM/browser/node)
- `host-parity/run-conformance` + `availability` + `guard-host-import`
- rule: host status `:no` → `:capability-absent` / `:host-absent` (never ambient success)
- browser `llm-infer` honest gap remains documented

## Implementation notes (2026-07-18 slice + P0/P1)

**P0 landed**
- strict-grammar opt-in via guest-grammar.edn (unknown heads → :unknown-form when enabled)
- compiler merges catalog forbidden-heads
- F-001: rad scaffold + mandatory package-lock already closed; `safe-release-ready?` added

**P1 landed**
- S4b `:policy/forbid-wildcard` → `:wildcard-forbidden` on :any intersection
- concrete-cap receipts unchanged (guard-call)
- `lang/host-parity.edn` + score (browser linkability ≥ 0.8)

## Implementation notes (2026-07-18 slice L1/L2)

Landed in the same change set as this ADR:

1. `kotoba-lang/lang/guest-grammar.edn` + `kotoba.lang.guest-grammar` loader
2. `kotoba.runtime/lower-language-forms`: string-literal host-arg lowering for
   registered string-head imports; multi-body `when` → `if`+`do`
3. `kotoba.runtime` unsupported-op / denied-form **hints** from the catalog
4. `compiler` frontend: `do` desugar + multi-body `when` via nested `let`
5. Regression tests + demo program for the new sugar

Follow-ups: wire both emitters to refuse forms not in the catalog under an
explicit `:strict-grammar` flag; advance L3 package/cap-value work.

## Consequences

- Authors get safer ergonomics without ambient power.
- Grammar drift becomes a catalog diff, not tribal knowledge.
- Fleet migration (2607171700) can point at real L2+ surface for guest cells.
